    d: [["Null hypothesis", "H₀, the model or parameter value tested as the default claim."], ["Alternative hypothesis", "H₁, the direction or difference supported if H₀ is rejected."], ["Significance level", "The maximum chosen probability of rejecting H₀ when it is true."], ["Critical region", "Test-statistic values that lead to rejection of H₀."], ["p-value", "The probability under H₀ of an outcome at least as extreme as observed in the direction(s) of H₁."], ["Type I error", "Rejecting a true H₀."], ["Type II error", "Failing to reject a false H₀ under a specified alternative."]],
    p: [["Setting up the test", "Define the parameter, write H₀ with equality, and make H₁ match the claim. 'Increased' gives an upper tail, 'decreased' a lower tail, and 'changed' two tails. The test calculation always uses the H₀ parameter.", ["Use population parameters, not sample statistics, in hypotheses.", "Choose the tail before seeing the result."]], ["Discrete tests", "For X binomial or Poisson, find the probability of the observed result or something more extreme under H₀. Reject if that p-value is ≤α. A critical region is chosen so its H₀ probability is at most α; discreteness means the actual size may be smaller.", ["For two tails, identify both extremes rather than blindly doubling if the distribution is asymmetric.", "State the actual critical-region probability when requested."]], ["Normal and mean tests", "Use a continuity-corrected normal approximation for binomial/Poisson when conditions hold. For a mean, standardise Z=(X̄−μ₀)/(σ/√n), using s for σ in a large-sample setting as allowed, then compare with the relevant critical value or p-value.", ["Put μ₀ from H₀ in the numerator.", "A two-tailed α test places α/2 in each tail."]], ["Errors and conclusions", "Type I probability is the rejection-region probability under H₀. Type II probability is the acceptance-region probability under a specified alternative. Finish with 'reject H₀' or 'do not reject H₀', followed by a contextual evidence statement—never say H₀ is proved.", ["Power=1−P(Type II error).", "The conclusion must use the direction in H₁."]]],
    f: [["Mean test statistic", "Z=(X̄−μ₀)/(σ/√n)"], ["Decision by p-value", "reject H₀ when p≤α"], ["Type I error", "P(rejection region | H₀ true)"], ["Type II error", "P(acceptance region | specified H₁ true)"]],
    r: [["Where does equality belong in hypotheses?", "In H₀."], ["What tail matches 'the mean has decreased'?", "A lower-tailed test."], ["What is a Type I error?", "Rejecting H₀ when H₀ is true."], ["How should a non-significant result be stated?", "Do not reject H₀; there is insufficient evidence for the contextual alternative claim."]],
    t: ["Write hypotheses and significance level before calculating probabilities.", "End with a decision and a separate sentence in the language of the question."],
